---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import ProductDirectory from "../components/ProductDirectory.astro";
const unified = process.env.PIT_UNIFIED_PREVIEW === "1";
---
<Layout title="PIT Web3 tools" description="Free local analysis, read-only blockchain inspections and separately isolated local operations.">
  <section class="hero product-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">PIT · Web3 tools with clear boundaries</div>
    <h1>Understand the data. Review the risk. Then choose an operation.</h1>
    <p>Explore free financial tools, public-chain inspections and locally tested token operations. Calculations need no wallet or account. Transaction tools require explicit wallet approval and remain restricted to local Anvil.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button-link" href="#directory">Find a tool</a><a class="button-link secondary" href="/guide/">How PIT works</a>{unified && <><a class="button-link secondary" href="/toolbox/">Open offline Toolbox</a><a class="button-link secondary" href="/explorer/">Open read-only Explorer</a></>}</div>
    <p class="notice">PIT fees are proposed, not live. The local payment demonstration uses MOCK-USDC only; Base Sepolia and mainnet payment execution are disabled.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-label="Ways to use PIT" class="product-lanes">
    <article class="panel"><small class="eyebrow">01 · Free</small><h2>Work privately in your browser</h2><p>151 offline task experiences use manual inputs. No wallet, account, subscription or background RPC.</p></article>
    <article class="panel"><small class="eyebrow">02 · Free</small><h2>Inspect public chains</h2><p>28 bounded read-only inspections. The selected public RPC provider can see addresses you submit.</p></article>
    <article class="panel"><small class="eyebrow">03 · Local prototype</small><h2>Prepare on-chain actions</h2><p>18 operational routes. Five creation and funding workflows also have an atomic mock-USDC payment path on Anvil.</p></article>
  </section>
  <ProductDirectory />
  <section class="panel"><h2>Fees, gas and permissions stay separate</h2><p>A proposed PIT fee is denominated in USDC. Network gas is paid in ETH. Token transfers and approvals are additional actions shown before signing; no exchange rate or combined currency total is invented.</p><p>Atomic local payment and operation either both succeed or both revert. Approval gas and reverted transaction gas are not automatically refunded. A confirmed transfer or token creation is generally irreversible.</p><a href="/operations/token-creator/">Review token creation →</a></section>
  <script src="../bootstrap.ts"></script>
</Layout>
